  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 4.443,
   "e": 6.513,
   "text": "The Modular Emergence Paradox.",
   "dur": 2.07,
   "voiced": 119,
   "sim": 0.749,
   "f0": 119.584,
   "st": -0.06,
   "range_st": 9.753,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 7.498,
   "e": 15.361,
   "text": "If self-organization, local plasticity, and continuous topological rewiring are the proven mechanisms of biological cognition,",
   "dur": 7.863,
   "voiced": 572,
   "sim": 0.87,
   "f0": 119.704,
   "st": -0.043,
   "range_st": 5.617,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 15.658,
   "e": 22.804,
   "text": "why did decades of research into dynamic neural graphs fail to produce modern foundational models?",
   "dur": 7.146,
   "voiced": 535,
   "sim": 0.83,
   "f0": 115.108,
   "st": -0.721,
   "range_st": 4.007,
   "asr": 0.897,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 23.816,
   "e": 25.153,
   "text": "And conversely,",
   "dur": 1.336,
   "voiced": 81,
   "sim": 0.656,
   "f0": 121.704,
   "st": 0.244,
   "range_st": 6.828,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 25.642,
   "e": 34.596,
   "text": "why did the Transformer, an architecture that violently rejects biological realism with its brute-force all-to-all attention matrices and uniform backpropagation,",
   "dur": 8.954,
   "voiced": 689,
   "sim": 0.861,
   "f0": 116.847,
   "st": -0.461,
   "range_st": 5.589,
   "asr": 0.894,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 35.148,
   "e": 38.869,
   "text": "conquer every single domain of modern intelligence?",
   "dur": 3.722,
   "voiced": 286,
   "sim": 0.657,
   "f0": 120.863,
   "st": 0.124,
   "range_st": 3.318,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 39.871,
   "e": 42.482,
   "text": "Examine the stark contradiction before us.",
   "dur": 2.611,
   "voiced": 166,
   "sim": 0.785,
   "f0": 115.735,
   "st": -0.627,
   "range_st": 4.998,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 43.416,
   "e": 48.204,
   "text": "Self-organizing networks promised organic modularity and continuous adaptation.",
   "dur": 4.788,
   "voiced": 346,
   "sim": 0.829,
   "f0": 115.479,
   "st": -0.665,
   "range_st": 5.489,
   "asr": 0.889,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 48.783,
   "e": 58.552,
   "text": "Yet in practice, as these networks scale, they inevitably collapse into representational chaos, destructive interference, or catastrophic forgetting.",
   "dur": 9.769,
   "voiced": 482,
   "sim": 0.687,
   "f0": 127.11,
   "st": 0.997,
   "range_st": 7.66,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 59.319,
   "e": 65.317,
   "text": "Meanwhile, the Transformer, constructed from static, dense, homogeneous matrix multiplications,",
   "dur": 5.998,
   "voiced": 374,
   "sim": 0.856,
   "f0": 118.148,
   "st": -0.269,
   "range_st": 5.756,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 65.617,
   "e": 69.376,
   "text": "spontaneously discovers internal modularity.",
   "dur": 3.758,
   "voiced": 210,
   "sim": 0.829,
   "f0": 119.996,
   "st": -0.001,
   "range_st": 5.569,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 70.154,
   "e": 75.154,
   "text": "Inside a trained Transformer, researchers in mechanistic interpretability have uncovered",
   "dur": 5.0,
   "voiced": 344,
   "sim": 0.807,
   "f0": 124.485,
   "st": 0.635,
   "range_st": 8.495,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 75.495,
   "e": 85.371,
   "text": "sophisticated induction heads, modular routing circuits, arithmetic units, and in-context associative recall mechanisms.",
   "dur": 9.876,
   "voiced": 556,
   "sim": 0.727,
   "f0": 121.676,
   "st": 0.24,
   "range_st": 4.882,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 86.287,
   "e": 91.681,
   "text": "These functional circuits emerge entirely without any dynamic topological rewiring during inference.",
   "dur": 5.394,
   "voiced": 442,
   "sim": 0.863,
   "f0": 117.629,
   "st": -0.345,
   "range_st": 6.359,
   "asr": 0.833,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 92.28,
   "e": 94.833,
   "text": "The weights remain completely fixed,",
   "dur": 2.553,
   "voiced": 140,
   "sim": 0.64,
   "f0": 117.941,
   "st": -0.3,
   "range_st": 5.149,
   "asr": 0.8,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 95.035,
   "e": 101.62,
   "text": "yet the activation flow exhibits extraordinary dynamic routing and multi-step algorithmic execution.",
   "dur": 6.585,
   "voiced": 449,
   "sim": 0.774,
   "f0": 118.787,
   "st": -0.176,
   "range_st": 5.648,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 102.6,
   "e": 109.72,
   "text": "In seminal work by Olsson and colleagues, attention heads coordinate across layers to form induction circuits,",
   "dur": 7.12,
   "voiced": 443,
   "sim": 0.82,
   "f0": 119.991,
   "st": -0.001,
   "range_st": 7.307,
   "asr": 0.938,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 110.247,
   "e": 113.583,
   "text": "which appear to be a mechanistic source of in-context learning.",
   "dur": 3.336,
   "voiced": 246,
   "sim": 0.791,
   "f0": 118.613,
   "st": -0.201,
   "range_st": 4.016,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 114.673,
   "e": 120.11,
   "text": "When an induction head operates, it copies previous tokens based on bilinear query-key matching,",
   "dur": 5.437,
   "voiced": 372,
   "sim": 0.846,
   "f0": 123.065,
   "st": 0.437,
   "range_st": 7.678,
   "asr": 0.966,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 120.359,
   "e": 123.395,
   "text": "effectively retrieving arbitrary associative context.",
   "dur": 3.035,
   "voiced": 183,
   "sim": 0.792,
   "f0": 117.863,
   "st": -0.311,
   "range_st": 3.204,
   "asr": 0.8,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 123.8,
   "e": 130.247,
   "text": "Biologically-inspired local plasticity rules cannot perform this token-specific lookup without catastrophic interference.",
   "dur": 6.447,
   "voiced": 474,
   "sim": 0.826,
   "f0": 116.336,
   "st": -0.537,
   "range_st": 4.977,
   "asr": 0.929,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 131.264,
   "e": 142.067,
   "text": "How could a rigid, non-biological monolith spontaneously evolve the very modular reasoning that biologically-inspired self-organizing networks failed to produce?",
   "dur": 10.803,
   "voiced": 802,
   "sim": 0.66,
   "f0": 116.046,
   "st": -0.58,
   "range_st": 3.947,
   "asr": 0.955,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 142.287,
   "e": 147.965,
   "text": "This paradox cannot be explained away by dataset size or engineering patience alone.",
   "dur": 5.679,
   "voiced": 387,
   "sim": 0.84,
   "f0": 118.2,
   "st": -0.262,
   "range_st": 4.756,
   "asr": 0.923,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 149.072,
   "e": 153.872,
   "text": "To understand why self-adapting networks failed where Transformers succeeded,",
   "dur": 4.8,
   "voiced": 318,
   "sim": 0.829,
   "f0": 123.436,
   "st": 0.489,
   "range_st": 7.298,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "s": 154.201,
